atisfied with  the steps that i'm taking to to work on  that um  is this something that  results from our own efforts or are we  satisfied and it's more something that  happens to us that's something to think  about the other two  blessed  and inspired these are not things that  you can produce in yourselves if the  words really mean what they're supposed  to mean  you can't make yourself blessed  that's a gratuitous gift  inspired i would say is along the same  lines it's kind of  there's a kind of weirdness to somebody  sort of inspiring themselves or making  themselves inspired we get inspired by  other things and their effects on us  they're unpredictable  excessive going beyond the normal  boundaries effects on us so those are  those are other ones and then there's  two that i left till the very end  one of these is spiritual spiritual is  one of those terms that really could be  all sorts of things all over the map but  i think that my in my view there really  is a strong connection between  spirituality and i by that i don't mean  spiritual not religious i think that  much of spirituality uh has been  developed through religion i'm not  saying that the two things are identical  but um you know great spiritual  practices many of them came out of the  matrices of religious belief but also  religious life and religious community  and so happiness is something that they  are concerned with what does it take to  actually be happy what is the nature of  happiness how do i attain it and a lot  of these other things you're going to  see being given as advice you want to be  happy give to other people that's that's  something that you can find in buddhism  christianity judaism all across the  map  and then the last one that i'm going to  close on happiness one of the types of  happiness  that they talk about in this 31 types is  love  now love is such a grand term i actually  you know spent an entire semester with  my students you can see the videos on  that in intro 